  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1022 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nSurface ridging will settle into the area on Sunday bringing much \nlower temperatures to the region. At the same time, short wave \nridging will build overhead with flattening flow by early Monday. A \nmuch weaker short wave will approach the area on Monday but will \nagain lead to breezy surface winds. Surface cyclogenesis in lee of \nthe Rockies will develop in response to this short wave bringing \nsouthwesterly downsloping winds. The cool down on Sunday will be \nshort lived with the downsloping winds boosting temperatures back \nabove seasonal averages on Monday afternoon. The semi-permanent lee \ntroughing will continue for Tuesday as another short wave moves \nonshore in southern California. Further warming will occur on \nTuesday with continued downsloping winds. The next main point of \ncontention in the forecast will be this now closed off low moving \nacross the southwestern US mid-week. Models have not been consistent \nin the track of this system as it approaches the area around \nWednesday to Thursday next week. At the moment, it looks like this \nsystem will be able to draw a significant amount of low level \nmoisture into the area. but it remains to be seen if this will \ntranslate into measurable precipitation before we are dry slotted.",
